<title>USA: Pharmacia, Solvay win FDA nod for Luvox.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia, Solvay win FDA nod for Luvox.</headline>
<dateline>MARIETTA, Ga. 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc, and Solvay Pharmaceuticals Inc said on Tuesday that their Luvox product won U.S. Food and Drug Administration clearance to treat obsessive-compulsive disorder in children.</p>
<p>Luvox already is used to treat this condition in adults, the companies said. An estimated one million children and adolescents also suffer from this disorder, they said.</p>
<p>Luvox is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor.</p>
</text>
